      "origin": "Quadimara",
      "passive_list": {
        "0": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<p>(HP+5 , MP+5 , IP+2)<br>Permanently increase your maximum Hit Points and maximum Mind Points by 5.Choose one option: gain the ability to equip martial melee and ranged weapons, martial armor, and martial shields; or learn any one spell from the Elementalist or Spiritist lists; or permanently increase your maximum Inventory Points by 2</p>",
          "passive_name": " SURVIVOR",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "quirk"
        },
        "1": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<ul>\n<li>Yourself or one ally<br>            You spend your time looking for useful items; describe how, then roll 1d6.<br>                    1. Ouch! You do not recover Hit Points and Mind Points during this rest.<br>                    2. Not what I was looking for... The target regains 1 Inventory Point.<br>                    3-5. Hoho, this can be useful! The target regains 3 Inventory Points.<br>                    6. Jackpot! You find an amount of zenit equal to 【your character level × 50]</li>\n</ul>",
          "passive_name": "Exploration ",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "camp activity"
        },
        "2": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<ul>\n<li>Once before the next rest, if the target is about to pay a Mind Point cost, they may <br>halve that MP cost. This benefit cannot be applied to a Ritual's MP cost.</li>\n</ul>",
          "passive_name": "Massage ",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "camp activity"
        }
      },
